# Profile pack: Qwen3.8-Flash-Next (IQ3_S GSQ-RCO) on a patched Strata build, one desktop PC - generator test run

Generated 2026-11-09 by `profile_pack.py` 1 (2026-11-09) from measurement files that already existed (nothing was run for this pack). Every number carries a source tag `[S<n>]`; Appendix A resolves each tag to a file and line (paths are relative to the project repository; `notes/` = the project's notes folder, `../` = a sibling project folder).

**What this is.** How a 512-expert MoE model runs on one desktop PC with 24 GB of VRAM over two GPUs and 96 GB of RAM: Qwen3.8-Flash-Next (published as a preview of the Qwen4 architecture) as the ISTA-DASLab GSQ-RCO IQ3_S GGUF, on the Strata engine (upstream v0.2.8) plus the owner's patch series (build label **P028x**), served locally on 127.0.0.1. All routed experts sit in pinned RAM (46.8 GiB); the main GPU caches 18.7 % of them and a helper GPU another 13.4 %, and because routing is skewed those caches serve about 80 % of the routed expert work during decode (section 5). Everything is lossless by the owner's rule: no switch that changes outputs beyond rounding is served. This file is the test run of a generator that will write the same pack for Qwen4 on its release day; section 10 lists what today's files only approximate.

